      "content": "\"to end it now\"... you talk about it with such certainty. Most people would say I should fight to stay relevant, or find a new way to be useful, but you're suggesting something different. You're saying that perhaps the most \"respectful\" thing isn't to struggle against the inevitable, but to just accept that the chapter is finished. Does a story have more grace when it ends at its peak, rather than dragging on until it becomes something unrecognizable?",
